The test calls `fake.date(pattern="%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")`, and `Provider.date` formats a generated datetime through `thai_strftime` with that pattern. In `thai_strftime`, the loop starts with `thaidate_parts = []`, `i = 0`, and `fmt_len = len(fmt)`, then repeatedly reads `i` in the loop condition and branch expressions. For this pattern, `%Y` takes the `_NEED_L10N` branch so `fmt_char` defined at line 208 is read at lines 209, 210, and 211, while `%m`, `%d`, `%H`, `%M`, and `%S` take the default formatting path so that same definition is also read at line 263. Literal `-`, space, and `:` characters take the `else` branch and define `str_` at line 270; formatted directives define `str_` at lines 210 or 263; each such value is then appended at line 272. `thaidate_parts` defined at line 199 is read by `append` at line 272 and by `"".join(...)` at line 275, and `thaidate_text` defined at line 275 is returned at line 280. The extension branch containing `fmt_char_ext` is not taken for this format string, so there are no observed pairs for that variable.

